 ## Overview
-Gradient-based Pre-computed Shading is a preprocessing technique that computes shaded colors for each voxel using a view-independent Lambertian shading model, allowing for faster rendering by avoiding per-ray normal computation [S1, S2, unofficial]. It differs from on-the-fly gradient estimation by trading memory for performance, storing the shading result in an additional 3D texture, which implicitly applies a low-pass filter to gradients [S3].
+Gradient-based Pre-computed Shading is a preprocessing technique that computes shaded colors for each voxel using a view-independent Lambertian shading model, allowing for faster rendering by avoiding per-ray normal computation [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial]. Unlike on-the-fly gradient estimation, which trades memory for performance during rendering via multiple dependent texture fetches [S3], this method precomputes the shading result into an additional 3D texture, which implicitly applies a low-pass filter to the gradients during trilinear interpolation [S3].
 
